# vfc-site line-ending policy. Added 2026-09-06.
#
# WHY. Every push warned `LF will be replaced by CRLF`. The repo had no
# .gitattributes and relied on core.autocrlf=true, which is a per-machine
# setting: it lives in the clone, not in the repo, so it cannot follow the
# tree and it is silent when it is missing. `* text=auto` puts the policy in
# the repo itself. LF in the object store, native in the working tree.
#
# Leann approved `* text=auto` on 2026-09-05 and deferred the session.

* text=auto

# Text, normalised to LF in the object store.
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.js    text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.csv   text
*.xml   text
*.txt   text
*.svg   text

# Binary. Never touched, never diffed as text. A newline rewritten inside a
# PNG or a font is silent corruption, which is the whole reason this list is
# explicit rather than left to git's content heuristic.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
